{
  "note": [
    "Shared conformance fixture for gm's two implementations: the Rust core and",
    "the browser editor. Both test suites read this file and must agree.",
    "",
    "It exists because two implementations of the same rules drift, quietly, and",
    "the way you find out is an engineer saving a file in the editor that",
    "`gm commit` then refuses. Hue vectors keep a material the same colour in",
    "both; the validation case keeps 'what is an error' the same in both.",
    "",
    "The document deliberately avoids two rules that cannot be exercised through",
    "a round trip: a layer referencing an undefined material, and two layers at",
    "the same level. Both are caught, but the materialised tables reject them",
    "before the validator is reached, so they are tested separately."
  ],
